From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h6: orangepi-3-lts: Enable AC200
 codec

The OrangePi 3 LTS has the AC200's analog audio codec populated, same
as the plain OrangePi 3 it's based on (its reg_aldo2 regulator is even
still named "vcc33-audio-tv-ephy-mac", carried over unchanged from the
board it derives from). Unlike the plain OrangePi 3, though, this
board doesn't use the AC200's Ethernet PHY at all - &emac here is
wired to a Motorcomm RGMII PHY instead - so &ac200 itself was never
enabled at all, missing entirely rather than just missing its
codec/sound children.

ac-ldoin-supply, ephy-vcc-supply, rtc-vcc-supply and tv-vcc-supply are
all required properties on the AC200 mfd node regardless of which of
its functions are actually wired up on a given board (see
Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/x-powers,ac200.yaml), so all
four still need to be set here even though ephy-vcc/tv-vcc go unused.

Signed-off-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../sun50i-h6-orangepi-3-lts.dts             | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h6-orangepi-3-lts.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h6-orangepi-3-lts.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h6-orangepi-3-lts.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h6-orangepi-3-lts.dts
@@ -99,6 +99,25 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&ac200 {
+	ac-ldoin-supply = <&reg_aldo2>;
+	ephy-vcc-supply = <&reg_aldo2>;
+	rtc-vcc-supply = <&reg_aldo2>;
+	tv-vcc-supply = <&reg_aldo2>;
+};
+
+&ac200_codec {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ac200_sound {
+	simple-audio-card,widgets = "Microphone", "Onboard Microphone",
+				    "Line", "Line Out";
+	simple-audio-card,routing = "MIC1", "Onboard Microphone",
+				    "Line Out", "LINEOUT";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &cpu0 {
 	cpu-supply = <&reg_dcdca>;
 };
@@ -146,6 +165,14 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&i2c3 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&i2s3 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &mdio {
 	ext_rgmii_phy: ethernet-phy@1 {
 		compatible = "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c22";
